 consistently within single digits would warrant moving this toward Likely R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Cotton (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Tom Cotton seeks a third term in a state that has trended firmly Republican, with a partisan lean of about fifteen points to the right. Hallie Shoffner, a former farmer and biotech executive, has drawn attention with a campaign built around the farm financial crisis and has raised a credible sum for a first-time candidate, but she trails badly in money and faces outside spending against her.\n\nPolling has been sparse and inconsistent: a Hendrix College survey showed Shoffner slightly ahead, while a J.L. Partners poll gave Cotton a sixteen-point lead, and averages of other races suggest a mid-single-digit to low-double-digit Cotton edge. Every major race rating places this in Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets put Cotton's chances above ninety percent. The fundamentals point to a comfortable Cotton win, with some room for the race to tighten if the farm-crisis message resonates.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0277, "margin": -11.06}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0629, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0436, "margin": -11.0}]}